Ziyun Su is pursuing a M.S. under the supervision of Dr. Fuqin Zheng at Guangxi Normal University. Her scientific interests focus on the design and synthesis of metal-organic framework-based materials and their electrochemical applications.
Qiupin Huang is currently a B.S. in Guangxi Normal University under the supervision of Dr. Fuqin Zheng. Her research mainly focuses on the design and synthesis of electrocatalysts.
Qian Guo pursuing a master’s degree under the supervision of Prof. Wei Chen at Guangxi normal university. His scientific interests focus on the synthesis and property studies of metal nanoclusters, and the design and application of nanostructured electrocatalysts in ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}{\mathsf{R R}}.$
S. Jafar Hoseini received his Ph.D. in inorganic chemistry from Shiraz University in 2008 under the supervision of Prof. Mehdi Rashidi. Also, in the course of his studies, he moved to JawaharlalNehruCentreforAdvancedScientificResearch(JNCASR)to work on the synthesis of inorganic nanostructures under the supervision of Prof. C. N. R. Rao. He then worked as a professor at Chemistry Department of Yasouj University. He is currently a full professor at Chemistry Department of Shiraz  University.  His  research  interests  include  organoplatinum  chemistry,  inorganic  nanostructures,  electrocatalysts, metal-organic frameworks and application of nanomaterials in energy storage and conversion.
Fuqin Zheng received her B.S. degree in 2011 from Yanshan University and got her Ph.D. under the supervision of Prof. Wei Chen at Changchun Institute of Applied Chemistry, Chinese Academy of Sciences. She is currently working in School of Chemistry and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Guangxi Normal University. Her scientific interests focus on the design and synthesis of electrochemical catalysts, such as metal-organic frameworks, metal nanoclusters, and their application in energy storage and conversion.
Wei  Chen received  his  Ph.D.  in  electrochemistry  from  Xiamen  University  in  2003.  Following  his  graduate  studies,  he began working as a postdoctoral associate in the area of synthesis and property studies of metal nanoclusters at the University  of  California,  Santa  Cruz.  He  then  worked  as  professor  at  Changchun  Institute  of  Applied  Chemistry,  Chinese Academy of Sciences. He is currently a full professor at School of Chemistry and Pharmaceutical Sciences, Guangxi Normal University. His research interests include electroanalytical chemistry, surface electrochemistry, electrocatalysis, photoelectrocatalysis, and the controlled synthesis, characterization, and application of nanomaterials in energy storage and conversion.
